.TH HIROD 8 "August 2026" "HIRO" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
hirod \- HIRO face-authentication daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hirod
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR]
[\fB\-\-init-keys\fR]
[\fB\-\-prewarm\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBhirod\fR owns the IR camera, the ONNX face models, and the encrypted
template store. It serves the PAM module and the \fBhiro\fR(1) CLI over a
Unix socket (default \fI/run/hirod/hirod.sock\fR) and enforces rate limits,
lockouts, camera pinning, and audit logging.
.PP
The daemon must run as root. Start it via systemd:
.B systemctl start hirod
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --config PATH
Configuration file (default \fI/etc/hiro/config.toml\fR).
.TP
.B --init-keys
Create the encryption key file and template database, then exit. Run once
after installation.
.TP
.B --prewarm
Warm the models and camera, then exit (install-time check).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/hiro/config.toml
Configuration (see \fBhiro.conf\fR(5)).
.TP
.I /var/lib/hiro/templates.db
Encrypted template store (SQLite).
.TP
.I /var/lib/hiro/hiro.key
AES-256 data key, root-only.
.TP
.I /usr/share/hiro/models
ONNX model files.
.SH AUDIT
Every verdict is logged to the journal under the \fIhiro_audit\fR target:
.B journalctl -t hirod -g hiro_audit
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hiro (1),
.BR pam_hiro (8),
.BR hiro.conf (5)
